{"id": "EUVD-2026-6171", "enisaUuid": "c44215ad-9ab0-32cb-8f30-357b0a229ac0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvmet-tcp: add bounds checks in nvmet_tcp_build_pdu_iovec\n\nnvmet_tcp_build_pdu_iovec() could walk past cmd->req.sg when a PDU\nlength or offset exceeds sg_cnt and then use bogus sg->length/offset\nvalues, leading to _copy_to_iter() GPF/KASAN. Guard sg_idx, remaining\nentries, and sg->length/offset before building the bvec.", "datePublished": "2026-02-13T13:29:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:25:31", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b9981751be14b59b4473383c731c833738aebdb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42afe8ed8ad2de9c19457156244ef3e1eca94b5d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1385be357e8acd09b36e026567f3a9d5c61139de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dca1a6ba0da9f472ef040525fab10fd9956db59f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/19672ae68d52ff75347ebe2420dde1b07adca09f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab200d71553bdcf4de554a5985b05b2dd606bc57", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/52a0a98549344ca20ad81a4176d68d28e3c05a5c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jjrf-jfrm-p64x", "CVE-2026-23112"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "031d7ae5-3310-3666-a3dc-7edb987b6c19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.70"}, {"id": "079ca07b-a9c1-32c6-9782-291b622c464c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.10"}, {"id": "15940e3d-6c22-3300-92ba-45dcf7310c99", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.253"}, {"id": "1b439a2c-ea15-3dd1-8d30-7a2f7d8056e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "872d26a391da92ed8f0c0f5cb5fef428067b7f30 <42afe8ed8ad2de9c19457156244ef3e1eca94b5d"}, {"id": "351e336